0..66 Comment "// Theory inclusion: `include` extends a presentation by another\'s"
67..138 Comment "// members, the included ones first, and keeps the inclusion beside the"
139..207 Comment "// value. A monoid is a semigroup with a unit; two extensions of the"
208..283 Comment "// semigroup included together meet along it, so the result has one carrier"
284..357 Comment "// and one multiplication (the pushout over what they share). The union\'s"
358..431 Comment "// rules are completed as the block\'s own: the included associativity and"
432..454 Comment "// the unit laws join."
455..457 Comment "//"
458..472 Comment "// - see: #738"
